-- Search reads the same text, folded as FTS5 folds it, on every provider.
-- D1: every FTS5 table's four triggers index each column's text as every
-- provider reads it (search-index.ts, searchColumnTextSql): a rich-text
-- column (a product's or category's description, a page's content) without
-- its markup, the first 10,000 characters, the zero-width joiner and
-- non-joiner ignored and the precomposed Bengali nukta letters decomposed.
-- Then the rows whose indexed text changes are indexed again: every row of a
-- table with a rich-text column, elsewhere only the rows holding a character
-- the index now normalises or a column past 10,000 characters. The tables
-- keep their external content: never run FTS5's 'rebuild' on them.
-- Turso: the marker expands into the search index's refresh
-- (searchIndexSqliteRefreshStatements): the fold table, every trigger
-- (one per indexed column, so a name edit never re-reads a description), and
-- the index rebuilt. External providers upgrade under the verified write freeze.
DROP TRIGGER IF EXISTS `products_fts_after_insert`;
